WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:03.033
-Kit, last time you were here.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.434
First of all,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.434
Last time you were here,
we did a bit called

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.868
"Kit Harington Straight Up
Goes For It."

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.133
-Yes.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:13.100
-And you just sang
"Drops of Jupiter" by Train.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.234
That was the whole bit.

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.968
We asked probably
30 different celebrities

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:20.033
to do this throughout our years
being on the show.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.133
And everyone said, "No."

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:26.400
You're the only one
with the guts to do it.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:32.701
-And I will never forget that.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:35.534
And I just want to know
from this appearance,

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.634
did you get any offers?

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:39.934
Just tell us what's up.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.734
-Worryingly few, actually.

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:42.868
-You didn't get anything?

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:45.934
-Not a single offer
of anything musical,

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.901
which was surprising to me,
actually.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:52.300
I got a few texts
from friends and family.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.534
-That's nice.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.367
-They didn't know
quite why I did it.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.100
-Did they not --

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.968
But the best is
I go to you, I go,

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.200
"Kit, do you want
to do this bit?"

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.067
And you go, "Yeah, I don't
really sing."

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.234
I go, "That's the whole point.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.334
That's exactly what we want."

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.801
-And then I got in here,
and you were like, "No one --

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.534
We've been asking people
to do this for years.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.534
No one's done it,"
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.267
-Oh, yeah. I didn't want
to tell you --

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.234
I didn't want
to tell you that then.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.234
I waited till you did the bit,
then I told you the truth.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.667
Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:20.667
How's your son doing?

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.901
-He's good. He's 2.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.367
He's -- yeah, we think he's --

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.901
we think he might be
quite smart.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:27.934
-Ooh.
-Which is...

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:29.167
-Oh, that's good.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:30.400
-That's a good thing.
-Well, it's surprising,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.300
seeing as we're both actors.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.000
No, we're like,
we're not sure where

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.868
that's -- quite where
that's come from.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.100
-You don't want him
to be an actor?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.734
-Well, we -- like,
he loves applause.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:40.968
We like --

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.934
We sort of, every time
he does something good,

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:44.968
we give him applause,
and we're worrying

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:47.734
that's kind of pushing him
towards acting.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.100
We're a bit like,

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.934
"Eh, you might be too smart
for this, you know,

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:51.934
go save the world.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.400
We're sick, we had no choice.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.167
-Yeah.
-But he's really good.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:02:00.934
He's about to get the shock
of his life, which is that

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.868
he's about to get
a brother or sister.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.367
-Are you serious?

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.234
Congratulations. No way!

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.501
-Oh, yeah.
-Pregnant?

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:09.934
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.801
Thank you.
-That's fantastic.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:12.968
You got a new baby coming.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.234
That's unbelievable!
-I know, I know.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.868
Yeah --
-Are you excited?

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.133
Are you nervous?
-I'm so -- I'm terrified.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.601
Like, I --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.501
You know, with the first baby,

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.133
you're, like, walking on clouds

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.934
and dancing through fields
of daisies for nine months.

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:27.400
-Yeah.
-Well, the man is, anyway.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.534
[ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.434
-But this time you go,

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:34.267
like the reality check
comes much shorter.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.400
You're, like,
you get practical real quick.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.267
-Yeah, because you know what's
in store.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.767
-Yeah, two of them.
-And what does you son think

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.367
about the new baby?

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.767
-I'm not sure
he's quite conceptually

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.767
understood it just yet.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:50.501
He, like -- we're trying
to get him ready for it.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:54.934
We point at Rose's tummy,
and we say, "Mommy's baby.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.501
Mommy's baby."
-That's right.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.801
-And he points at his tummy
and goes, "My baby."

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:04.868
-I'm quite sure that's --
that's, yeah, well,

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:07.834
you'll know soon enough.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:10.567
I saw that you recently attended

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:13.501
the "Game of Thrones" convention
in Los Angeles.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:14.501
-Yeah.
-That's a --

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:17.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.234
What is that like for you
to go to those things?

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.501
It was like, it was a bit
like going back in time.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.167
You know, I know it's only been
four years or something,

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.200
but it feels longer.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.067
And I went to it,

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:30.467
and it's nice seeing the fans,
and it's kind of amazing

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.701
that that show
has still got such a fan base,

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.033
and it's continuing on
in its own way.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.634
-Well, I mean,
there's rumors out there

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.634
that there's a there's
a "Game of Thrones" spin-off

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.100
that features your character,
Jon Snow.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.834
Is it happening?

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:47.868
-Well, I don't know.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.767
Do you want to have it?

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.367
[ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.467
Yeah, I do want to have it.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.534
I do want it.
I think people would love it.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.534
-Yeah.
-I'd love to see you

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:58.567
as Jon Snow.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:02.367
-Yeah, I can't say
anything on that,

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:07.100
but I don't know, man, like.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.000
-Well, what -- what would stop
you from doing it?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.634
Do you miss it at all?

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:14.734
-I walked down the street, and,
you know, I get recognized

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.868
a little less nowadays, and...
-Oh, wow.

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.467
-...and it kind of hurts my ego,
you know.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.501
No, I'm pretty close to,
like, putting on some furs, but.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:26.934
-So it would --

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:30.934
So what would it take for you
to do this spin-off series?

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:33.501
Would it take -- Do you want us
to ignore you?

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:35.567
-Yeah, I think, like,
I've got a tally

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:39.734
in my head of how few photos
I get asked for in a day.

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:41.434
-Mm-hmm.
-And when it gets below

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.968
a certain number,
I think I'll do the spin-off.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:43.968
Yeah.
-All right.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:46.901
So fans of Kit Harington,

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.501
do not ask him for a photo
for the next --

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:51.300
If you do for the next two days,
by Monday,

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.234
we could have an answer,
and we could see

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.667
a "Game of Thrones" spin off
right now with Jon Snow,

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.434
all right?
We'll do this together.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:05:01.067
We'll do it together.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.868
Let's talk about your new movie,
"Baby Ruby".

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:06.834
Congrats. You play
a new dad in this film

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:08.734
when you were actually
a brand-new dad.

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:10.133
Did that help you
with the performance?

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:11.934
-Yeah, that was another level
of insanity.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.901
Like, I left,
I mean, think about this --

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:18.667
I left a screaming child
at home to go and do a movie

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:21.434
about a screaming child.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:22.667
-What's wrong with you?

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:26.100
-There's, like --
and on this set, you had twins.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.767
So if one stopped screaming,
they'd bring the other one on.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:32.434
You can't pinch your child
anymore, isn't it?

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:33.968
-Yeah, yeah,
you don't do that anymore.

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:35.367
-It's not allowed.
-No.

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.968
-Yeah.
-So that's wild.

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:39.601
But so you do this film,
which, by the way, it is --

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:42.067
it's a thriller, it's scary.

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:43.234
-Yeah, it's a kind of thriller.

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:46.434
It's a horror thriller
comedy thing.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.167
-Yeah, kind of.
-You're allowed to laugh.

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:49.834
-You're allowed to laugh
at it a little bit, yeah.

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:52.367
-It's funny.

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:53.834
So it follows --

00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:57.701
it's about postpartum psychosis
and about the lack of care

00:05:57.701 --> 00:06:00.834
that mothers get after birth.

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:02.300
And so that's
an important message.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.601
But it's really --
it's really not about me.

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:06.801
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:08.767
-I had to put my ego aside.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:09.901
It's not about you
for this one, yeah.

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:11.634
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.367
Here's Kit Harington
in "Baby Ruby".

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:14.767
Take a look at this.

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:16.367
-Who wants Ruby?

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:18.434
-[ Breathing heavily ]

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.267
You're still wearing your apron?

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:30.567
-Yeah, well, your message,
it said you're in danger,

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:33.133
so I came as fast as I could.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:35.167
And she's okay,

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:39.567
so no more sneaking around
where you don't belong.

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:42.734
Stay here. I'm gonna
go upstairs and get cleaned up.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:48.701
You're gonna stay right here.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:52.767
And then when I come back down,
we can talk, okay?

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:55.067
You're gonna by okay?
-Yes, sure.

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.167
-Good.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:03.334
-Whoa! Come on!

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:04.801
Kit Harington, everyone.

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:08.133
"Baby Ruby" is in theaters
and on demand now.

